  "id": "Compound::DB00679 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Thioridazine is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through a series of interconnected pathways involving parotid swelling and its binding to cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Thioridazine, through its role in causing parotid swelling, is linked to desipramine or amitriptyline, both of which bind to Cyp2c19. These findings highlight a potential mechanism where Thioridazine may influence Cyp2c19 activity via the parotid swelling pathway, possibly through the indirect effects of these compounds. The shared lowest common ancestors—Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound and Agent Affecting Nervous System—suggest a broader pharmacological context, emphasizing the role of these compounds in modulating enzyme activity. The integration of these pathways underscores a possible dependency on the nervous system, with Thioridazine potentially acting as a mediator in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through parotid swelling and its associated compounds.",
